orative fireplace, while offering a bright and contemporary living environment. Extending to over 645 sq ft, the property is well proportioned and enjoys an abundance of natural light. To the front of the property are a spacious reception room and separate kitchen whilst at the rear, two south-facing double bedrooms provide a peaceful retreat. The principal bedroom features a fitted wardrobe offering excellent storage, while the second bedroom is equally suited as a guest room, home office or study. A stylish family bathroom is centrally located, and further built-in storage is available from the hallway. Offered part-furnished or unfurnished, the property provides flexible accommodation ideal for professionals, couples or small families.<br /><br />This attractive area of South West London has retained its distinctive character and village-like feel, offering a peaceful residential setting while remaining well connected. Just a short stroll away, Tooting Bec Common provides an extensive green open space, perfect for walking, running, outdoor exercise and summer picnics.<br /><br />The area benefits from an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars and leisure facilities, combining a relaxed neighbourhood atmosphere with all the conveniences of modern London living. Well-regarded local schools include Henry Cavendish Primary School, Broomwood Hall and Streatham & Clapham High School. Transport links are excellent, with Balham Underground Station (Northern Line) and Streatham Hill station both within easy reach, providing convenient access to Central London and beyond. Brixton Underground Station (Victoria Line) is easily accessible via the frequent 24-hour bus services along Streatham High Road.<br /><br />** HOW TO ARRANGE A VIEWING: The quickest way to enquire about this property is to register your interest via the enquiry button on this website. We will send you an email a moment later with an online enquiry form for you to complete. You will then be conta